{"id": "clm:753017bc431d5a69aae9cf4d9f8e59a317be0b589e3b873b604b4b311a947045", "type": "statement", "text": "The locked percentage is a legacy global write-lock field that appears only against MongoDB versions before 3.0. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "definition", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:afa567ba3c3854c0d2d481a7a65e777af5ce0efd45f897226b784620eccd08e8"]}
{"id": "clm:d2c10baa0dc7178b559dc38384d068f46fe55b1d6bed9675146ed255fa86bfe3", "type": "statement", "text": "mongostat normalizes operation statistics to average operations per second even when the polling interval exceeds one second. Read operation rates separately from connection counts and memory snapshots. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2a331483c52afebde754647d02bdad7938168edc94435b63a4e6fd0ffb735475", "ev:70111f52a42279c28cf47bbbc2041b4974e72fd8da050bf99587981c7d6980a7", "ev:e80324a9c1899e64440da44cd4b4e7b3824b1d31cb9bf616bb005a05ed0ecec0"]}
{"id": "clm:b84445d8033bd93fa72acb060e4ab00e0eb5dde2dd499f0eecf9cf7bc38c549a", "type": "statement", "text": "mongostat set gives the replica-set name when applicable; repl gives member state: PRI primary, SEC secondary, REC recovering, UNK unknown, RTR mongos router, and ARB arbiter. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:845ea89ebbd2e3f191cb039452f7aa93a2cb2601d21f32b97081dadfbcd02a0a"]}
{"id": "clm:f35597402974588efc93a4b766c8900a512ded4ea87dcec5f9a249a85c022a7c", "type": "statement", "text": "mongostat --discover can return statistics for all members when connected to a sharded cluster through mongos; the examples also combine --discover with --interactive for a non-scrolling view. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat/mongostat-examples.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:3c49770f3c1dfb10994a20cf583609b0be63be9c23ed03dd335516d38a356747"]}
{"id": "clm:4288abcd068b75f9652c048adfe434186d305ca4a64d63fdbb2d54d21f67c8ec", "type": "statement", "text": "CloudThinker uses mongotop as a per-collection, per-interval workload view and separates queued readers/writers from active readers/writers when reading mongostat. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://cloudthinker.io/blogs/mongodb-performance-audit-native-tools", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:fd1a9a3901d969ff68461c5a2d41e64ed43292780bd2daf92b00d77a0e770f95"]}
{"id": "clm:20033d429fd2912c6c9ea559918a7c7643f2265363b66e7b1f42dfd236443eb0", "type": "statement", "text": "mongostat vsize reports process virtual memory and res reports process resident memory, documented in megabytes at the last call. conn reports the total number of open connections. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2a331483c52afebde754647d02bdad7938168edc94435b63a4e6fd0ffb735475", "ev:e80324a9c1899e64440da44cd4b4e7b3824b1d31cb9bf616bb005a05ed0ecec0"]}
{"id": "clm:08db8744c97a635800478ac6a54b7e930f089a38764cd39edb142805c63b6425", "type": "statement", "text": "For WiredTiger, flushes counts checkpoints triggered between polling intervals. This field is an interval count rather than a checkpoint-duration measurement. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:c10bc41e5697c8475be6ed7d2c3c77c149f2265052bbf6de4ea5c1e3036911c3"]}
{"id": "clm:02ad47851081e3d78f258304b9f443d6cb9bbfda4350b29a7b5482227339b458", "type": "statement", "text": "vsize reports process virtual memory, whereas res reports process resident memory. The reference describes these as memory amounts at the last mongostat call, rather than operation rates. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://genexdbs.com/introduction-to-mongodb-diagnostic-tools-mongotop-and-mongostat/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2a331483c52afebde754647d02bdad7938168edc94435b63a4e6fd0ffb735475", "ev:c6d330e711ec07e1e812ce6dbb7ec576e1fa1a96b3433d9b7f174866adb769c7"]}
{"id": "clm:0cb9f7875c288885a4d167b0d8c43267a3e04942b7f30488dfc2008f9ed76be8", "type": "statement", "text": "mongostat gives an instance-level status overview; mongotop locates read and write activity at the collection level. Use the two views together to relate node pressure to busy collections. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongotop.md", "https://software.danielwatrous.com/mongodb-monitoring-with-mongostat/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:803f21cbd664afe1871700748fb8ae8a7c43d7bb5efc438054f023a0d52ba2fc", "ev:afdf3d2bf1afadea1449e5ec66745d3a14a2bf77a6dba8ad585daaf35e02f42c", "ev:b4569ced42ca14c196e4f203895daf7eb9a3634edf1d1be929c5dafdf66b4c75", "ev:cdf193f2f054d9beb059d906acbbc886adc9d64c3141584d74e7cb61ca56cee6"]}
{"id": "clm:308ab9828eb9c1e58de165c7d9f31b225ffd71c3aafb38ee5dc9c965697af413", "type": "statement", "text": "The operation columns report inserts, query operations, updates, deletes, cursor-batch getmore operations, and commands per second. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://genexdbs.com/introduction-to-mongodb-diagnostic-tools-mongotop-and-mongostat/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2cb9a2fd7ad530b85f2a88ece99304d2db9306c9de6718c646d0005cba53fa17", "ev:a1e495455ce578562880ecd47922e92ed36109790281609ab7ee91fa8a3ab9ca"]}
{"id": "clm:214e71c070cf649c6ccb3003a3c7fe5cf5b1ed17fdd0dfac4189f9a0e1cb9ee3", "type": "statement", "text": "An asterisk on the insert value denotes a replicated operation. On a secondary, command values separated by a pipe represent local|replicated commands. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2cb9a2fd7ad530b85f2a88ece99304d2db9306c9de6718c646d0005cba53fa17"]}
{"id": "clm:dcc09d2a0707f4c5000bfd5602e7fe8896c8d33ebe7e23b1c0fa2b114b3caf51", "type": "statement", "text": "For WiredTiger, dirty is tracked dirty bytes divided by maximum configured cache bytes; used is current cache bytes divided by maximum configured cache bytes. Both are cache percentages, so interpret them against the configured WiredTiger cache. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:31facad635434b26ec825132195d6861217161feccd089bfd58bf021a6a1998e"]}
{"id": "clm:f1c75c3d09f80891d3f1df409c6a79bdee0e0d9f35882f41d4fd511fa7a3697c", "type": "statement", "text": "mongostat qr and qw are queue lengths for clients waiting to read and write; ar and aw count active clients performing reads and writes. The paired output headings qrw and arw distinguish queued from active readers and writers. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://cloudthinker.io/blogs/mongodb-performance-audit-native-tools", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat/mongostat-examples.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:170f3770a1155c13ec1151bd6f4ae1ab849468e693ab86bea4392f64d949d65a", "ev:af336823bb0fc3d360f14b31070ea8261219a19db09ab170cb052b4425305bb5"]}
{"id": "clm:65510e5cd3168549c12af3d4904eec0826740fbca28b4e2bde28c52e9382ca37", "type": "statement", "text": "netIn and netOut measure incoming and outgoing network traffic in bytes, including traffic generated by mongostat itself; conn is the total number of open connections. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7056e9f8b54e50ec781d20a79ffb0d366b2293a50efbce7e95e8b30f7a697e05"]}
{"id": "clm:c76ee78d0364b784abeed091da94b393bf801519296a502ac64d1897ed0a6e3c", "type": "statement", "text": "mongotop time values are milliseconds. ns combines database and collection names; total is time spent operating on the namespace, while read and write report time spent performing the respective operations. The timestamp dates the returned data. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongotop.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://genexdbs.com/introduction-to-mongodb-diagnostic-tools-mongotop-and-mongostat/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:795cdbfc7f4b2e7a565c1fea867f35f407f76319e289faf316e6bfce456a1293"]}
{"id": "clm:b85d31290436b266614e60cc9811d9c84ae58e224761e9ea952dec4485ad57b8", "type": "statement", "text": "mongotop reports active namespaces or databases. If a collection or database is absent, the documentation says it has received no recent activity. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongotop.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a5440c7b62131b212c681009441af39530b30cb071c1f2e2dfde2d8ac0c856c8"]}
{"id": "clm:950db7935b5435c6e4e106953f558daf73eab5e7932bdad21a7c8d222a04d6bb", "type": "statement", "text": "mongotop --json adds operation counts for the polling interval to the timing data. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongotop.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:8f8150e8c18122ea13f9dc2cf5b9dc088ae0eaed467d20f3fafa3ec80a990b66"]}
{"id": "clm:073242bb6eb48e2f7de3b860768bac2ddab1c8e22fc543a0ca8536ce80d7d60f", "type": "statement", "text": "mongotop --locks is historical: it reports per-database locks only for MongoDB 2.6 or older and errors on 3.0 or newer instances that do not expose that data. In this mode db replaces ns, and database name . denotes the global lock. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongotop.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:ada2624f50a5ac1d96921a9527d97dba3a182c2c3e41b8eb1d60d9ae224a727c", "ev:c27d940ec6aafaf3bc88c6983d356add44e63effb09357bd2ba9635999b307dc"]}
{"id": "clm:644598d92296fcd4bb6ae4daef3ce8e14b4f62a0f73628a179fd2cd4b3cea392", "type": "statement", "text": "mongostat -o selects the output columns; -O adds serverStatus fields after the defaults. The options are mutually exclusive. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat/mongostat-examples.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:417230ee0b63ce06c1e359bfcbe606ede6ff6710d0d97ccba91cb1b81b052b56", "ev:60070dea349473e25e0aeb6e9322158cc12d242ccc5c910d6f427150859744f2"]}
{"id": "clm:6aee8ee79ddcbc3bda4a2f0e04fe52e9b260baf0cfe0c88043d6fde1cb3b4199", "type": "statement", "text": "For custom numerical serverStatus columns, .rate() reports the per-second change and .diff() reports change since the previous sample. The official examples demonstrate both in the -o field expression. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat/mongostat-examples.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:771601292c6a68fec9cb10242c9ad18fce90563cbbadd9bb122c0990153b3681", "ev:e921cd832536b998f8b54da554c48d190b5cb16add6876e180db4ae2fc7d14d6"]}
{"id": "clm:5504fff01996f09ca9366a7f10eee6c6d41426567581001681e7fdb91229eaef", "type": "statement", "text": "The historical Stack Overflow discussion cautions that operation-rate interpretation depends on the server configuration and cluster architecture; its example throughput numbers are not universal capacity limits. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/13522241/interpreting-mongostat-and-mongotop-output", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0628f01f9eeff48e0cbf5f86115d29aadcb3c2edc5939ac626d137d0da61a158"]}
{"id": "clm:05822daad1ce81f2048ed27aa6cc77354f98de132cb0c07d730e4708805b2d6b", "type": "statement", "text": "The mongostat inserts field counts inserted objects per second; query, update and delete count operations per second. getmore counts cursor-batch operations per second. An asterisk after an insert value denotes a replicated operation; secondary command values use local|replicated. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2cb9a2fd7ad530b85f2a88ece99304d2db9306c9de6718c646d0005cba53fa17"]}
{"id": "clm:334b4fbd843ba285ee1cc88da23a8f5fb272b980f7afccb2dba4c60f4ab159f4", "type": "statement", "text": "mongostat netIn and netOut describe received and sent network traffic in bytes, including traffic generated by mongostat itself. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7056e9f8b54e50ec781d20a79ffb0d366b2293a50efbce7e95e8b30f7a697e05"]}
{"id": "clm:93ce951c5fdeb86d81d8a71ff3886ac1dd7b513fced09fbaf7fbb95c6d3a071d", "type": "statement", "text": "mongotop reports read and write activity per collection and accepts a reporting interval in seconds; its default reporting interval is one second. Use its per-collection view to locate where read and write time is concentrated. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongotop.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://cloudthinker.io/blogs/mongodb-performance-audit-native-tools"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:54f2c79900d2202d7cc51fd468b0c01c452f80de469e2164efaf7fdc9ab4e1d8", "ev:92251fce48644897a03cb9ec07a50bdbbc3e088fcb019f3e0470583a91888c80", "ev:fb5162f96b668ec165e6be95af468a18a8f8d6e3bf0519ecb9d1d3ef091d449b"]}
{"id": "clm:f6c3ee913d1c422eb764ce2d3b3c9f288054a12a9efa1afbb0d02385ff3dd8f2", "type": "statement", "text": "Historical lock fields need server-version context: mongostat locked appears only for pre-3.0 servers. mongotop --locks needs MongoDB 2.6 or older and errors on MongoDB 3.0 or newer servers that do not report per-database lock usage. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongostat.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["mongostat and mongotop fields and how to read them"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongotop.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1ea18a93bb3df703fa90cd546497f0e48941a878774a07d417ce667770229b6b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:afa567ba3c3854c0d2d481a7a65e777af5ce0efd45f897226b784620eccd08e8", "ev:c27d940ec6aafaf3bc88c6983d356add44e63effb09357bd2ba9635999b307dc"]}
